    date "2022-02-01T12:19:54Z"
    title "The Best Abs Workout (Upper Abs, Lower Abs, Obliques)"
    description "To develop any muscle to its fullest growth potential, you need to move through a variety of angles and use different rep ranges &#8211; and your abs are no exception. Yes, you first must shift that spare tyre for them to show, but simply getting lean doesn&#8217;t mean you&#8217;ll have a solid and sculpted six-pack. For that you need to train your upper, lower and side abs both hard and smart, which is what this circuit session will do&#10;&#10;0:00 Lying Leg Raise&#10;0:35 Lying Legs Hold&#10;1:20 Wipers (straight legs)&#10;1:55 Oblique Crunch&#10;2:40 Frog Crunch&#10;3:16 Cocoons Crunch&#10;4:01 Hip Lift with Head up&#10;4:36 Lying Legs Hip Raise&#10;5:21 Circle Leg Crunch&#10;5:57 Criss Cross Leg Raises&#10;6:42 Crunch (leg raise) &#10;&#10;#sixpack #6packabs #obliques #abs #abworkout&#10;&#10;ab workout at home ab workout for women ab workout routine ab workout for men ab workouts with dumbbells ab workout no equipment ab workout gym&#10;What is the best workout for abs?&#10;What are the top 5 ab exercises?&#10;Is a 10 minute ab workout effective?&#10;How can I get abs in 2 weeks?"
